From 8a147efafbbf60d492d7ae1f18af5627e4a7d03c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: azorkai <e.guven@hotmail.com.tr>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 17:24:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ASoC: amd: acp-config: add DMI quirk for Huawei MateBook
 M1080

The Huawei MateBook D16 identified by board vendor "HUAWEI", product name
"HVY-WXX9" and product version "M1080" carries the same AMD Renoir ACP
block wired to an ES8316 codec as the MateBook revisions already listed
here (M1010, M1020, M1040), but none of the existing entries match its
DMI strings.

Without a match snd_amd_acp_find_config() does not return
FLAG_AMD_LEGACY for this board, so the legacy ACP backend is never
selected, the acp3x-es83xx platform device is never created, and the
machine ends up with no analog playback path at all - only the HDMI
codec shows up in aplay -l and the internal speakers stay silent.

Add an entry for the M1080 revision, identical in shape to the existing
MateBook entries, so the legacy ACP path is selected on this board too.

Signed-off-by: azorkai <e.guven@hotmail.com.tr>
---
 sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
index 0d977f4..4282707 100644
--- a/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c
@@ -183,6 +183,20 @@ static const struct config_entry config_table[] = {
 			{}
 		},
 	},
+	{
+		.flags = FLAG_AMD_LEGACY,
+		.device = ACP_PCI_DEV_ID,
+		.dmi_table = (const struct dmi_system_id []) {
+			{
+				.matches = {
+					DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "HUAWEI"),
+					DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "HVY-WXX9"),
+					DMI_EXACT_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_VERSION, "M1080"),
+				},
+			},
+			{}
+		},
+	},
 };
 
 static int snd_amd_acp_acpi_find_config(struct pci_dev *pci)
